# Token-Saving Toolkit Mode

MANDATORY: When working in AI_Agents directory, ALWAYS use runbook toolkit for modifications to save tokens:

## When to Use Toolkit
- ANY file modifications (edit, write, create)
- ANY system configuration changes
- ANY multi-step operations
- Operations involving 3+ tool calls

## When Standard Tools Are OK
- Single file reads for inspection
- Simple queries (ls, status checks)
- One-off commands without side effects

## Toolkit Usage
- Tool calls: 17-26 → 3-4 per operation (80% reduction)
- Use: python -m runbook_toolkit execute --plan /tmp/artifacts/PLAN.json --artifacts-dir /tmp/artifacts
- Path: /home/user/AI_Agents/runbook_toolkit

## Process
1. Create PLAN.json with all operations
2. Execute toolkit with plan
3. Verify results

## Toolkit Development
- After using toolkit for new operation types, consider:
  - Adding reusable templates to /home/user/AI_Agents/runbook_toolkit/templates/
  - Updating AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS.md with new patterns
  - Improving toolkit modules if operation reveals gaps
- Document new runbooks in /home/user/AI_Agents/runbook_toolkit/runbooks/
